<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.1.1>	Iam nunc per omne lux refulget saeculum,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.1.2>	Lux illa, patris quae lucet de solio,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.1.3>	Quae fons, origo, splendor lucis aureae
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.1.4>	Habensque semper lumen indeficiens
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.1.5>	Caelum serenat arcens mundi tenebras.
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.2.1>	Huius sacrato lucis de uibramine
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.2.2>	Suscepit almum radium sub pectore
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.2.3>	Marcus beatus, doctor euangelicus,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.2.4>	Factus lucerna, more tanti luminis
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.2.5>	Ardens fugauit saeculi caliginem.
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.3.1>	Aureis septem unum de candelabris
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.3.2>	Cingitque totum mundum claro sydere,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.3.3>	Septem columpnis una de candidulis
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.3.4>	Ecclesiarum nititur sub culmine,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.3.5>	Sustentat altae fundamenta fabricae.
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.4.1>	Quartum quod olim uiderat Hiezechihel
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.4.2>	Propheta sanctus, animal lectissimum
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.4.3>	Uidit Iohannes seu Christi recubitor
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.4.4>	Leonis recte tipice sub specie
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.4.5>	Clamore multo per deserta frendere.
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.5.1>	Sic a beato Petro missus adiit
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.5.2>	Aquileiensem dudum famosissimam
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.5.3>	Urbem, sacrati uerbi pullulantia
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.5.4>	Disseminauit sata, quo centuplices
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.5.5>	Fructus ad alta uexit felix horrea.
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.6.1>	Christi dicauit mox ibi ecclesiam,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.6.2>	Nam fundamentum fidei fortissimum
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.6.3>	Fixerat unum petram super limpidam,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.6.4>	Quam flumen undans nec uentorum fulmina
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.6.5>	Quassare possunt, torrentes nec pluuiae.
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.7.1>	Deinde rursus cum corona remeans
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.7.2>	Athleta Christi compta pulchris liliis
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.7.3>	Mixtumque palmis, lauro atque rosulis,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.7.4>	Portabat gaudens dyadema uertice,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.7.5>	Ingressus urbem Romam Christo comite.
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.8.1>	His ita gestis pergit Alexandriam
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.8.2>	Sancto repletus spiritu, latissimos
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.8.3>	Fines per omnes iugiter Memphiticos
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.8.4>	Patris tremendi praedicabat unicum
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.8.5>	Uenisse mundi pro salute filium.
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.9.1>	Turba crudelis Christi circa militem
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.9.2>	Tumens parabat tormentorum spicula,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.9.3>	Uincxit catenis, transfixit aculeis
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.9.4>	Dilaniando flagris sancta uiscera,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.9.5>	Carceris umbras misit ad phantasticas.
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.10.1>	Primus superni nominis notitiam
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.10.2>	Dedit in urbem Marcus Alexandriam,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.10.3>	Christi dicauit mox ibi basilicam,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.10.4>	Quam expiauit pretioso sanguine,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.10.5>	Uallauit almae fidei munimine.
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.11.1>	Gloria patri, decus et imperium
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.11.2>	Sit, nate, semper tibi super sydera,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.11.3>	Honor, potestas sanctoque spiritui,
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.11.4>	Sit trinitatis uirtus indiuiduae
<paulin_aquil. carm. 13.11.5>	Per infinita seculorum secula.
